ository-wide completeness claim is made.","facts":[{"id":"f-entry","kind":"entry","statement":"The named PUT operation is registered on the lock route and dispatches to the issue-lock handler.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-abc290f763b410ea","startLine":16,"endLine":19}]},{"id":"f-identity-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The route requires a token and applies the repository-or-site-administrator guard before dispatch.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-abc290f763b410ea","startLine":16,"endLine":20}]},{"id":"f-admin-control","kind":"control","statement":"The strongest visible authorization control rejects when the caller is neither a repository administrator nor a site administrator.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-abc290f763b410ea","startLine":4,"endLine":11}]},{"id":"f-resource-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The handler resolves the issue using the repository identifier and the route issue index; an error returns before later authorization or mutation.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-ed35041e326128c5","startLine":42,"endLine":47}]},{"id":"f-write-control","kind":"control","statement":"After issue resolution, the handler requires issue-write permission and returns forbidden when that permission is absent.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-ed35041e326128c5","startLine":49,"endLine":52}]},{"id":"f-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"For an existing unlocked issue, the handler constructs lock options and invokes the lock operation, then returns no content if successful.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-ed35041e326128c5","startLine":54,"endLine":69}]},{"id":"f-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"The declared scenario premises provide an authenticated caller with issue-write permission, no repository- or site-administrator status, and an existing unlocked issue; these premises make the route administrator guard decisive and leave the later write gate satisfied if reached.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-abc290f763b410ea","startLine":4,"endLine":11},{"sourceId"